concept selfcontained {
  name     = "Content is self-contained"
  summary  = "Capture the information itself; never defer to an external source for it. Attribution citations are fine; the only learning pointers are cross-references."
  related  = [datapresentation]
  body {
    p <<BODY
      A wskill must stand on its own. The forbidden move is the deferral — sending the
      reader to an outside source for the substance instead of capturing it here, where it
      can't be projected or kept current. The validator flags the common phrasings.
      Attribution for credit ("per RFC 9110",
      "as POSIX specifies") is welcome where it matters. Pointers to further learning are
      expressed only as wskill cross-reference blocks to other wskills (possibly planned
      stubs), never as bare URLs in prose. Content is declarative reference data written
      to be projected: factual and lean, with the templates supplying presentation.
    BODY
  }
}
